ggvis integrates reactivity into its API in a way we're not likely to see again, I think. Not because it's wrong, but because it's quite difficult to implement and the implications on the package's code go very deep. Similar to how ggplot2's aes specifications and + were successful yet you didn't see any imitators, yet %>% has caught on like wildfire.

