You should make your filtering step into a reactive expression; it's a good idea in general, and essential if you want to use the same calculated data from two different outputs (i.e. the table and plot). See here:
http://shiny.rstudio.com/tutorial/lesson6/

I'm not sure what you mean by "same width of cells". Are you saying you want them side-by-side, or just for the table to span the entire width? For the latter, you can do this with CSS but probably easier and better to use dataTableOutput/renderDataTable instead of tableOutput/renderTable.

