eval(parse()) is indeed how you would do this, BUT it is only suitable for use when the person who is using the Shiny app is also the person who launched the Shiny app--in other words, for single-user use on one's own computer, not for hosting via ShinyApps.io or Shiny Server. The reason is because eval(parse()) will let the user execute arbitrary code on the machine that's running server.R--for example, "unlink('/', recursive = TRUE)".

