The issue is how Shiny loads. When you start the application the tab that the plot is located under is not visible. Because of this, the value that the plot begins with is NULL because there is nowhere and nothing to plot. You need to pass a dummy value to get rid of the NULL passed from session$clientData$output_plot_out_width. Here is the code you are looking for.

library(shiny)

shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {

  rv <- reactiveValues()
  rv$plot_out <- FALSE

  observe({
        input$plot_type
        rv$plot_out <- FALSE
    })

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    observe({
        rv$plot_out <- input$plot_button
    })

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  react<- reactiveValues(h = 200)

  output$plot_out <- renderPlot({
    if (rv$plot_out == FALSE)
      return(NULL)

    plot(cars, type = input$plot_type)

  }, height = function() {

        if(!is.null(session$clientData$output_plot_out_width)){
          return(session$clientData$output_plot_out_width)
        }
        return(react$h)

  })

  outputOptions(output, "plot_out", suspendWhenHidden = FALSE)

})

 I hope this helped. Good Luck!

Amber

